     "\r\n<font face=\"georgia\" size=\"2\"><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>Dear all,</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>If you&#39;re interested in making your R analyses fully reproducible, we are offering </span><strong><span>2 discounted seats</span></strong><span> for researchers from </span><strong><span>low- and middle-income countries</span></strong><span> in our upcoming online course:</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><strong><span>An R Reproducibility Toolkit for the Practical Researcher</span></strong><br><strong><span>20–23 July </span></strong><span>(online)</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>Course website: <a href=\"https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/r-reproducibility/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/r-reproducibility/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792454838445000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3R4bcT2mQ-wCkwMNOafcZr\">https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/r-reproducibility/</a> </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>The course covers practical tools and workflows for reproducible research, including </span><strong><span>Quarto, Git &amp; GitHub, research compendia, renv, and Docker</span></strong><span>, helping you build transparent, shareable, and long-lasting R projects.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>If\r\n you are eligible and would like to apply for one of the discounted \r\nplaces, please get in touch. We&#39;d be delighted to hear from you.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>Best regards,</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>Carlo</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia;font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia;font-size:small\"></span></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:trebuchet ms;font-size:10pt\">--------------------<br><br>Carlo Pecoraro, Ph.D<br><br><br>Physalia-courses DIRECTOR</p></font>\r\n\r\n"
